      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Moderation is key, but when dealing with MAOIs, those tyramine levels can add up quickly, so even small amounts need careful consideration. It's best to keep the intake of intensely aged cheeses and cured meats very low, treating them as rare flavor accents rather than staples. If you feel too anxious about limiting foods, focus on nutrient-dense, low-tyramine protein sources like eggs and fresh poultry instead.",
      "source": "target",
